From 71a4c67de04283eca6da75e4cb838de319a5d8f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SpicyEggSalad <177426835+SpicyEggSalad@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:48:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] gpu: texture replacement packs and a texture dump

Every uploaded texture gets a key: a hash of its first level's guest bytes
with its format, size and palette. textures/<key>.png anywhere under the
executable's folder replaces it at any size, with a mip chain built from
it (WIC on Windows, the splash PNG decoder elsewhere). XBE_TEXTURE_DUMP
writes each replaceable texture once to textures_dump/<key>.png (DXT1/3/5
and every format DecodeLevel knows, as uncompressed RGBA PNGs), so a pack
starts from the title's own pictures. Rect textures only take a
replacement of their own size, being sampled in texels; cube maps,
volumes and video frames are never keyed. Both backends.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
